From: j7 gpu
Subject: j7 g3d: a late completion is not a dead slot (and no fail-fast poison)

The 2026-11-11 log answers it.  The dump taken at the moment the client was told -1 shows

    job_irq raw=00000002 ... js_status(+24)=00000008 js_cmd(+60)=00000000

so the tiler chain *did* complete on slot 1: bit 1 of JOB_IRQ_RAWSTAT was set, the start command had
been taken, and no fault was recorded anywhere.  Two of my own changes then turned that into a wall
of failures: the "slot looks stopped" early-out fires at 150 us, before the completion interrupt
lands, and the fail-fast counter it armed made the next sixty-four waits return -1 without ever
looking at the register.

Drop both.  Wait up to 20 ms (still returning the instant the interrupt lands), look once more for a
late completion before failing, clear the whole interrupt word so a stale bit cannot fake the next
chain, and log the first eight waits with the microseconds they took, so the next log states what a
real chain costs instead of what a broken probe thinks.

